        <p>ried out in heavy cloth of excellent quality, and of a pretty fawn shade almost :approaching stone-colour. From the neck turned back a wide collar faced ' with velvet of the same shade, • and edged ' with tit strapping of the cloth. The coat fastened down the front in double-breasted, Style, and was decorated with two rows- of big pearl buttons. A line of :machining finished the edges of the coat all round. The Sleeves were :quite. plain, and were completed by a-, turn-back cuff of velvet to mach the collar. ' SOME FASCINATING TIUNKETS. There are some very fascinating: trinkets on the 'market this autumn, says , a • Globe writer. • One is the ring-watch. The ring is in gold, of the expanding. type familiar to us in brace- .' lets. In it is set a tiny watch, its dial about the size of a threepenny bit, and *set round with rows el jewels. Another pretty novelty is being Much used for engagement and wed- . ding presents. This :is a bracelet of flexible gold, ending in two golden hands 'cla3Ped each in each; : The woman's - hand is rvlotned With a jewelled bracelet of tiny, dimensions, - and even a ring at well. The same idea is car- ried out even in, rings, when, -fitly though the ' clasped hands are, a 1 .;:vvel is inserted Co suo,- . gest. a bracelet on the feminine wrist. A DAINT:i. CAMISOLE. .</p>
        <p>Pictured in our illustration i a dainty little camisole, which is specially intended for r wear</p>
        <p>- - - beneath the übivitous transparent blouse or corsage. Thi3 camisole fastens up the 'back, and leaves the deooration of the front quite unbroken. The original, which hails from a .famous lingerie, house, .was carried out in the finest of natnsook. Round the topof the much- cut-out decalletage and the armholes cazarte a</p>
        <p>frill of Valenciennes lace, below which was a band of , slotted beading threaded with pink ribbon. The - front of toe camisole was deco- rated with a big diamond-shaped motif of Valenciennes lace, and a delicate design worked in white embroidery. The fulness of the garment was taken , into a succession of short tucks at the waist, and the camisole was completed by a waist-band of slotted beading threaded with ribbon to match the top.</p>
