      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1908-11-07_WidnesExaminer_art0012" n="art0012">
        <head>H CHURCHMEN AND THE LICENSING BILL.</head>
        <p>H CHURCHMEN AND THE LICENSING BILL.</p>
        <p>The executive of the Church of England Temperance Society on Tuesday resolved--" That, in view of the present position of the Licensing Lill, and the amend- ments that have been made in that measure, the society should du all in its power tu secure the passing of the Bill through the House of Lords." The Standing Advisory Committee of the society will meet in a few days to draw up a letter which it is intended to send to the members of the House of Lords.</p>
