        <p>Mr. Alfred Slater of 28, South Street, Ashton- under-Lyne, gives his experience of Dr. Mors-Zs Indian Root Pills in the following clear and concise statement, that should carry weight with the most sceptical :—" May I be allowed • to gfve •my tistimony for Dr. Morse's Indian Root Pills. Por the last five years I have been :- troubled with weak, diseased kidneys; and a had liver, and have had no pleasure during this time. I tried many of ; the remedies that are on the market but none succeeded in curing my back. I was under the doctor a consider- able time, but at last he gave me up. About six months- a^o a neighbour named Saxe eay asked me if I had ever tried Dr. Morse's Indian Root Pills. I obtained a bottle and in three months I felt a bit of " Worth benefit from them. I still their persevered with them anal' can . weight in now say at the end of six. Gold!!- „ months I am completely' . cured. I now know - the pleasure of living such al I have not experienced for the last five years. / I wish every suffering man in Ashton knew of your refnedy. It has, .• been a Cod-send to me. I would not be without them. • They are worth their weight in gold to me. I shall recommend them to all my friend and relatives. I still take them regularly and find they .keep me in good health, and I am able to fulfil my duties as a collier, which you know is an occupation which entails a great amount of backwork, and I mil now free from all pain. You are at perfect liberty to publish this 'testimonial if you wish. Sold by Chemists and Stores, price 1/11 per . bottle, or The W. FL Comstock Co., Ltd., 21, Farringdon Avenue; London, E.C.</p>
