      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1908-11-07_WidnesExaminer_art0035" n="art0035">
        <head>Declined to Give Evidence.</head>
        <p>Declined to Give Evidence.</p>
        <p>Thomas Walsh of Ship vard, was charged at the Borough Polic.i Court on Monday with an aggravated assault on his wife Mary Walsh on Saturday night. About 12 o'clock on Saturday night a police officer was called to the house and found the woman suffer- ing from a severe head wound, alleged to have been inflicied by the defendant with a jug. When the case corns up for hearing the woman absolutely refused to give evidence against the man, stating that it was her fault. Joseph Cristo a hdger,at the house, stated that the wound was duo to a fall caused through. a Stool, on which the woman was sitting, tipping up. The magistrates were dissatisfied with this statement, and frequently asked the woman to give evidence, but she declined to do so. The Bench decided to adjourn the case for a week until she was prepared to make a statement.</p>
      </div>
